        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281">

                <pb facs="0602" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v14p1/pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.00/9–654: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 281<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in the
                        Philippines</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d281-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-09-06T14:49:00-04:00">September 6, 1954—2:49
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tedul 19. Eyes only Secretary from Acting
                    Secretary. I read your Dulte 5<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d281-f2"/> to the President a few minutes ago. His estimate and
                    conclusion agrees with your own. He feels it would be a great mistake to
                    undertake assist defense of Quemoy unless reasonably certain it can be held, and
                    in view of nearness to mainland and other factors he is inclined to question
                    ability to hold indefinitely, particularly if as seems likely Communists are
                    willing to accept very heavy casualties to gain political objective.</p>
                <p>I am having meeting tomorrow with Anderson
                    and Radford and will try to get firm
                    estimate and definite recommendations, which will be transmitted immediately to
                    you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
